  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits a persistent downward bias when recent history is volatile but sentiment remains near zero; true outcomes often recover significantly higher than the forecasted trend.",
    "Forecast fails to capture immediate mean reversion after sharp historical spikes, resulting in an undershoot of the true outcome's first few days.",
    "When sentiment shows mixed signals (0.20-0.40) amidst high volatility, the model incorrectly projects a slow linear uptrend instead of a volatile range-bound path.",
    "The 30-day horizon forecast systematically underestimates the peak magnitude of true outcomes by approximately 5-10% when recent history indicates strong upward momentum.",
    "Model ignores short-term sentiment spikes (e.g., 0.40) as catalysts for immediate price jumps, leading to a lagged reaction in the forecast trajectory."
  ]
}
